+- `onError` fires for every turn rejection: a rejection that is already an `Error` reaches the hook as the same instance, and any other thrown value — a string, a plain object, or `undefined` — is wrapped in an `Error` whose `cause` is the thrown value, while the original rejection still propagates to the caller unchanged ([validated by: wraps a non-Error rejection in an Error with cause for onError and rethrows the original rejection unchanged](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L53)).
 - `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and is passed `totalUsage` — the sum of the usage every provider call in the turn reported, not the last round alone ([validated by: sums the usage of every round, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L555)).

